%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 7c7c947f0ccabb24dbf991df8e9f6d4f, type: 3}
  m_Name: curriculum elementary TE
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  defaultQuestions:
  - QuestionText: According to NCFTE-2009, what is the central vision for teacher
      education in India?
    Options:
    - To produce teachers who can complete the syllabus on time
    - To develop humane, reflective, and autonomous teachers
    - To focus exclusively on pedagogical skills
    - To standardize teaching methods across India
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: The NCFTE-2009 criticizes traditional teacher education for its
      theory-practice dichotomy. How does it propose to bridge this gap in the curriculum
      structure?
    Options:
    - By eliminating theoretical components entirely
    - By reducing the duration of the course
    - By focusing only on practical skills
    - By providing longer, more meaningful school internship programs
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: Which of the following is a core component of the D.El.Ed. curriculum
      framework that reflects its vision of inclusive education?
    Options:
    - Advanced Theoretical Physics
    - Creating an Inclusive School
    - Educational Administration
    - Foreign Language Training
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: If a teacher education program includes a course on "Understanding
      the Self," it is most directly aligned with which vision of NCFTE-2009?
    Options:
    - Developing technological proficiency
    - Focusing on examination reform
    - Enhancing subject matter knowledge
    - Fostering teacher autonomy and identity
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: 'The ''Internship'' in a D.El.Ed. program is designed to be a period
      of:'
    Options:
    - Observing senior teachers without any participation
    - Intensive engagement with learners and the school environment
    - Vacation for student-teachers
    - Theoretical study away from schools
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: A key feature of the elementary teacher education curriculum structure
      is its organization into three broad curricular areas. Which of the following
      is NOT one of them?
    Options:
    - Perspectives in Education
    - Curriculum and Pedagogy
    - Engineering and Technology
    - School Internship
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: 'The vision of "connecting knowledge to life outside the school"
      from NCF-2005 is operationalized in teacher education curriculum through areas
      like:'
    Options:
    - Rote memorization techniques
    - Pedagogy of Environmental Studies
    - Advanced Calculus
    - Theoretical Psychology only
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: Critically analyzing the vision of NCFTE-2009, which of the following
      would be considered a major implementation challenge?
    Options:
    - Its focus on reflective practice
    - The gap between its progressive vision and the reality of most TEIs
    - Its emphasis on child-centered education
    - Its recommendation for inclusive practices
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: 'The ''Perspectives in Education'' component in the curriculum
      includes foundational knowledge from:'
    Options:
    - Only Psychology
    - Only Management Studies
    - Only Pedagogy
    - Psychology, Sociology, and Philosophy
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: How does the structure of the modern D.El.Ed. curriculum address
      the vision of making education more flexible?
    Options:
    - By prescribing a rigid, uniform syllabus for all
    - By incorporating thematic rather than textbook-based teaching
    - By eliminating all practical components
    - By focusing only on traditional assessment methods
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: 'The NCFTE-2009 emphasizes that teacher education should move from:'
    Options:
    - A discipline-focused approach to a culture-focused approach
    - A rigid to a flexible model
    - A teacher-centered to a learner-centered paradigm
    - All of the above
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: 'In the context of curriculum structure, ''Pedagogy of Mathematics''
      at the elementary level primarily aims to:'
    Options:
    - Train mathematicians
    - Develop fear of numbers in children
    - Make mathematics a joyful, meaningful activity
    - Focus only on advanced algebra
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: 'The ''Vision'' of teacher education as per curriculum documents
      is best described as:'
    Options:
    - A set of rules for teacher behavior
    - A blueprint for teacher recruitment
    - A philosophical statement about the ideal teacher and teaching-learning process
    - A list of prescribed textbooks
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: 'A teacher educator designing a curriculum for ''Language Acquisition''
      would base it on the NCF-NCFTE vision that emphasizes:'
    Options:
    - Rote memorization of grammar rules
    - A multiliteracy and multilingual approach
    - Using only the English language
    - Avoiding the mother tongue in the classroom
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: 'The ''School Experience Program'' (SEP) in the curriculum is structured
      to:'
    Options:
    - Replace the internship entirely
    - Focus only on administrative duties
    - Be a one-time observation visit
    - Provide a continuous engagement with the school context, beginning early in
      the program
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: 'The ''Critical Perspective on Education'' in the curriculum aims
      to enable teachers to:'
    Options:
    - Accept all educational policies without question
    - Critically examine socio-political contexts of education
    - Focus only on classroom teaching
    - Avoid engagement with community issues
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: 'Comparing the vision of NCF-2005 and NCFTE-2009, a core commonality
      is their emphasis on:'
    Options:
    - Standardized testing as the primary goal
    - Reducing the number of working days for teachers
    - Reducing the burden on the learner and connecting knowledge to life
    - Increasing the amount of homework
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: 'The ''Gender'' component in the teacher education curriculum is
      included to:'
    Options:
    - Reinforce existing stereotypes
    - Promote sensitivity and equitable classroom practices
    - Focus only on women's education
    - Separate boys and girls in classes
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: 'The ''Peace Education'' component in the curriculum structure
      aligns with the vision of building:'
    Options:
    - A competitive and aggressive society
    - A democratic and just society
    - A society focused only on economic growth
    - A religiously segregated society
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: 'A significant shift in the structure of the teacher education
      curriculum, as recommended by NCFTE-2009, is from a:'
    Options:
    - Annual to a semester system
    - Practical-focused to a theory-only model
    - Local to an entirely international curriculum
    - Flexible to a rigid model
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: 'The ''Art Education'' component in the curriculum is justified
      by the vision that:'
    Options:
    - Arts are a waste of academic time
    - Arts are essential for the holistic development of the child
    - Arts should be taught only by special teachers
    - Arts have no connection with cognitive development
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: 'The ''Vision'' section of curriculum documents primarily serves
      to:'
    Options:
    - Provide a detailed day-to-day lesson plan
    - Guide the overall goals and direction of the program
    - List the names of recommended authors
    - Specify the furniture for classrooms
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: 'In the curriculum structure, ''Understanding the Child'' as a
      core area is derived from the foundational discipline of:'
    Options:
    - Sociology
    - Philosophy
    - Psychology
    - Economics
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: 'The ''Pedagogy of Social Science'' at the elementary level, as
      per the vision of NCF-2005, should aim to:'
    Options:
    - Promote rote learning of dates and events
    - Develop critical thinking about social issues
    - Avoid discussing contemporary problems
    - Focus only on geography
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: 'The ''ICT'' component in the teacher education curriculum is envisioned
      as a:'
    Options:
    - Separate subject with no connection to pedagogy
    - Tool for enhancing the teaching-learning process
    - Replacement for the teacher
    - Mandatory programming course
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: 'A teacher education institution that allocates significant time
      for community engagement is aligning its curriculum with the vision of:'
    Options:
    - Isolating the school from the community
    - Establishing the school as the only knowledge center
    - Building a connection between the school and the community
    - Focusing only on urban communities
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: 'The ''Curriculum and Pedagogy'' area in the D.El.Ed. structure
      is primarily concerned with:'
    Options:
    - Foundational theories of education only
    - The 'how' of teaching specific school subjects
    - Management of school finances
    - Historical development of education in Europe
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: 'The ''Reading and Reflecting on Texts'' paper is included in the
      curriculum to develop:'
    Options:
    - Speed reading skills only
    - Exclusive focus on fictional literature
    - The skill of memorizing texts
    - Critical literacy and the ability to engage with diverse texts
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: 'The ''Health and Physical Education'' component reflects the vision
      of:'
    Options:
    - Focusing only on academic achievement
    - The holistic development of the child
    - Training Olympic athletes
    - Separating physical health from mental health
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: 'A key difference between the structure of an old TTC (Teachers''
      Training Certificate) curriculum and the modern D.El.Ed. curriculum is the
      latter''s emphasis on:'
    Options:
    - Apprenticeship model without theoretical underpinnings
    - A balanced integration of theory and practice
    - Theory-dominated approach
    - Eliminating the internship component
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: The 'Vision' of the elementary teacher education curriculum is
      most directly opposed to which of the following practices?
    Options:
    - Child-centered learning
    - Reflective teaching
    - Rote memorization and textbook-centric teaching
    - Inclusive education
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: 'The ''Craft'' component in the curriculum (like ''Work and Education'')
      is based on the philosophical vision of:'
    Options:
    - Mahatma Gandhi's Nai Talim
    - Exclusive academic learning
    - Western models of industrialization
    - Avoiding manual work
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: 'The ''Assessment'' component in the teacher education curriculum
      trains teachers to:'
    Options:
    - Use only year-end examinations
    - Use continuous and comprehensive evaluation (CCE) to support learning
    - Focus only on grading and ranking students
    - Avoid assessing students altogether
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: 'The ''Perspectives in Education'' section of the curriculum aims
      to provide teachers with:'
    Options:
    - A set of fixed answers to educational problems
    - A lens to understand the broader context and aims of education
    - Skills for stock market investment
    - Training in medical sciences
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: 'The ''School Internship'' is structurally placed in the curriculum
      typically:'
    Options:
    - At the very beginning of the program
    - In the final year, as a culminating experience
    - Sporadically throughout the program with a sustained block at the end
    - Only after the theoretical exams are over
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: 'The ''Environmental Studies'' (EVS) curriculum for elementary
      classes is taught as an integrated area because:'
    Options:
    - It is less important than other subjects
    - Children at this age perceive the world holistically
    - It is easier to examine
    - There is a shortage of subject teachers
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: 'The ''Vision'' of the curriculum, as per NCFTE-2009, expects a
      teacher to be a(n):'
    Options:
    - Passive technician implementing prescribed methods
    - Isolated professional working alone
    - Authoritarian figure in the classroom
    - Active, reflective practitioner and facilitator
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: 'The structure of the D.El.Ed. curriculum mandates a certain number
      of days for internship. This highlights the importance given to:'
    Options:
    - Theoretical knowledge
    - Field experiences and practical training
    - Written examinations
    - Vacation time
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: 'The ''Pedagogy of English Language'' at the elementary level focuses
      on:'
    Options:
    - Teaching complex grammatical structures first
    - Developing communicative competence
    - Ensuring perfect pronunciation from day one
    - Avoiding the use of the mother tongue completely
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: 'A curriculum that includes ''Drama and Art in Education'' as a
      pedagogical tool is based on the vision that learning should be:'
    Options:
    - A serious and silent activity
    - Focused only on individual work
    - Confined to textbooks
    - An enjoyable and creative process
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: 'The ''Philosophical Foundations of Education'' within the curriculum
      structure helps a teacher to:'
    Options:
    - Develop their own perspective on the aims and purpose of education
    - Memorize the biographies of philosophers
    - Ignore practical classroom issues
    - Focus only on Western philosophy
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: 'The ''Sociological Foundations of Education'' component enables
      teachers to understand:'
    Options:
    - The impact of social factors on education
    - Only the economic status of students
    - The chemical composition of materials
    - Advanced mathematical theories
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: 'The ''Vision'' of the curriculum documents is ultimately realized
      through:'
    Options:
    - Its international comparisons
    - The number of pages in the document
    - The complexity of its language
    - The quality of its translation into syllabi, textbooks, and classroom transactions
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: 'The ''Community Work'' component in the internship is designed
      to:'
    Options:
    - Keep student-teachers busy
    - Help teachers understand the socio-cultural background of their learners
    - Replace classroom teaching
    - Focus only on urban community surveys
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: The structure of the curriculum, with its focus on 'Inclusive Education,'
      directly challenges which of the following traditional practices?
    Options:
    - Collaborative learning
    - Segregation of children with disabilities
    - The use of teaching-learning materials
    - Formative assessment
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: 'The ''Peace Education'' component in the curriculum structure
      is a reflection of the constitutional value of:'
    Options:
    - Fraternity
    - Right to Property
    - Centralization of power
    - Uniformity
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: 'The ''Curriculum and Pedagogy'' area is typically subdivided into:'
    Options:
    - Pedagogy of individual school subjects (Language, Mathematics, EVS, etc.)
    - Foundational disciplines only
    - Management studies
    - Advanced research methodologies
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: 'The ''Vision'' of the curriculum expects a teacher to be a facilitator
      of knowledge rather than a transmitter. This shift requires a change in:'
    Options:
    - The physical infrastructure of schools only
    - The teacher's role and classroom processes
    - The number of working days
    - The salary structure of teachers
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: 'The ''School Internship'' includes activities like lesson planning,
      teaching, and assessment. This structure is designed to develop:'
    Options:
    - Theoretical knowledge of child psychology
    - Practical professional competencies
    - Administrative skills for becoming a principal
    - Expertise in educational policy-making
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
  - QuestionText: 'A critical analysis of the curriculum''s vision would conclude
      that its successful implementation depends most heavily on:'
    Options:
    - The quality and commitment of teacher educators
    - The color of the school buildings
    - The number of students in a class
    - The political party in power
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: curriculum elementary TE
